{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-005", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam's GDP growth forecast raised to 8.7% for Q3 2026", "content": "Vietnam’s GDP is forecast to grow 8.7 per cent year on year in Q3 2026, according to Standard Chartered. \nIndustrial production is projected to rise 13.2 per cent in September, while Q3 exports and imports are expected to increase 27.2 per cent and 40 per cent, respectively. \nThe bank maintained its full-year growth forecast at 9.5 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-gdp-growth-forecast-raised-to-8-7-for-q3-2026-313847-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-006", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Nylon 6 chips, caprolactam ease: Why is NFY yarn holding steady?", "content": "Nylon filament yarn prices in domestic China held mostly steady between September 18 and 28, 2026, despite softer upstream costs. \nNylon 6 chips and caprolactam eased modestly, weighed down by softer crude and feedstock costs after a brief US-Iran flare-up. \nNFY POY 86D/24F fell hardest, down 3.5 per cent, while POY 70D/24F rebounded to end 0.2 per cent higher. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/nylon-6-chips-caprolactam-ease-why-is-nfy-yarn-holding-steady--313849-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-007", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia-US trade rises 30% to $11.1 bn in Jan-Aug 2026", "content": "Cambodia-US goods trade rose 29.9 per cent to $11.11 billion in January-August 2026, with Cambodian exports accounting for over 96 per cent of the total, according to GDCE. \nShipments to the US increased 28.5 per cent to $10.68 billion, while imports climbed 77.7 per cent to $431.83 million. \nThe US remained Cambodia’s largest export market. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cambodia-us-trade-rises-30-to-11-1-bn-in-jan-aug-2026-313837-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-008", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Indian cotton yarn remains weak, prices down in Mumbai", "content": "Mumbai cotton yarn fell ₹1–2 (~$0.01–0.02) per kg as ICE cotton volatility, weak downstream demand and payment constraints curbed buying.\nTiruppur prices were stable, but slow weaving demand kept mills under pressure, with selling-rate cuts possible next month.\nGujarat cotton fell ₹500 (~$5.20) per candy as global cues and early arrivals weighed, while high moisture remained a concern.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-indian-cotton-yarn-remains-weak-prices-down-in-mumbai-313844-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-009", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s $884 mn jute revival: Can it replace plastic?", "content": "Bangladesh jute and jute-goods exports reached $883.7 million in FY2025-26, up 7.75 per cent; July-August FY2026-27 exports rose 37.09 per cent.\nTexPro shows yarn made up 68.9 per cent of the FY2025-26 jute basket, while jute held 11.5 per cent of comparable jute/PE-PP sack trade in 2025.\nThe 2026-31 strategy targets $1.64 billion in exports by 2031 and a 70 per cent value-added share.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-884-mn-jute-revival-can-it-replace-plastic--313839-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-010", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton edges up on firmer market participation", "content": "ICE cotton futures edged higher on Monday, supported by improved US export sales and firmer participation, while rising harvest progress and speculative long liquidation limited gains.\nDecember 2026 closed at 82.86 cents per pound, up 15 points; US Upland sales rose to 230,500 bales, the US harvest reached 17 per cent, and China will suspend State Reserve cotton sales from September 30.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-edges-up-on-firmer-market-participation-313835-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-011", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["growth", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia's GDP growth to slow to 3% in 2026 as exports ease: IMF", "content": "Cambodia’s GDP growth is projected to slow to 3.0 per cent in 2026 from 5.3 per cent in 2025, with decelerating garment exports among the drags.\nHigher energy costs, weak tourism and remittances, subdued demand and tighter finance point to softer sourcing conditions.\nThe IMF urges targeted fiscal support, agile monetary policy and financial-sector repair.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cambodia-s-gdp-growth-to-slow-to-3-in-2026-as-exports-ease-imf-313833-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-29-012", "date": "2026-09-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.38, "keywords": ["record", "growth", "increase", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam’s EU exports grow 26%, but compliance demands increase", "content": "Vietnam-EU trade rose 23.2 per cent year on year to €52.6 billion in January-July 2026, with exports to the bloc increasing 26 per cent to €45.6 billion. \nTextiles and garments were among the sectors recording strong growth, but exporters face tighter EU requirements on sustainability, packaging, traceability, forced labour and e-commerce, raising compliance pressures.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-eu-exports-grow-26-but-compliance-demands-increase-313825-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
